		Annotation {
		  SID			  "1198"
		  Name			  "Racked may still spill a little payload, but it should not be enough to be significant and TOA needs to "
		  "be able to induce a secure pfw weigh when racked by doing a small dump"
		  Position		  [335, 1569, 625, 1638]
		  InternalMargins	  [0, 0, 0, 0]
		  FixedHeight		  on
		  FixedWidth		  on
		  ZOrder		  -1
		}
		Annotation {
		  SID			  "1128"
		  Name			  "Note that this fast response payload flavor is really only being used for its upper bound, to detect whe"
		  "n its likely that payload spilled past the target.  It might be worse at this than something we could develop with"
		  " some more time and thought.  The current design might respond faster than the other payload flavor, but is still "
		  "probably pretty slow because the light filtering prior to the statistics stage means that the confidence interval "
		  "is always pretty large.  This means the payload has to spill farther past the target than we'd like before we can "
		  "detect it.  A possible improvement would be to replace the fast response payload flavor with something faster.  On"
		  "e idea is to use the secure payload flavor's upper bound minus some estimate of spilling that is based on live pay"
		  "load.  Or, an estimate of spilling that is based on some bespoke algorithm on live payload such as peak and trough"
		  " detection and processing."
		  Position		  [23, -524, 437, -385]
		  InternalMargins	  [0, 0, 0, 0]
		  FixedHeight		  on
		  FixedWidth		  on
		  BackgroundColor	  "[0.992157, 0.937255, 0.913725]"
		  ZOrder		  -2
		}
		Annotation {
		  SID			  "992"
		  Name			  "MIN here because payload can only have spilled, it can't have been added.\n\nIf paylod is spilling, then"
		  " the non-notch-filtered bound should react quickly.  If not, then notch filtered should gain confidence quickly du"
		  "e to filtering out resonance fluctuations.\n\nNote that even the non-notch-filtered flavor still cannot instantane"
		  "ously respond to payload spilling due to the low pass filter portion of the statistics estimation.  This is a pote"
		  "ntial area of accuracy improvement.\n\nThe min on the lower bound means that it will likely be following the non-n"
		  "otch-filtered lower bound because that one converges slower and so will stay lower longer.  This means we will be "
		  "slower to recognize that payload is above target.  That's acceptable because:\n1. TOA will tip again if we don't r"
		  "each a conclusion about what to do and the measurement period ends\n2. The bound is more conservative, reflecting "
		  "our uncertainty about how much payload might have spilled.  This is important for estimation of the dump increment"
		  " in the implement control.  If we incorrectly think that our lower bound is higher, we will think we can dump thro"
		  "ugh a larger angle to spill more payload in the next tip increment."
		  Position		  [2184, -524, 2552, -255]
		  InternalMargins	  [0, 0, 0, 0]
		  FixedHeight		  on
		  FixedWidth		  on
		  ZOrder		  -3
		}
